  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "There is currently an issue when a Steam account has already been used for an account link and you try to use it again for a link with a new account. If you try to create a new account with the Steam login, you will end up being prevented from doing so. At the moment there is not even a correct error message, just a general error message.\n\nAs you already know: To link a Steam account, you need to log in to Steam to create an empty Steam-VRChat account, which you then link/merge with the account created on the website.\n\nSteps for reproducing the error:\n\n1. create a VRChat account using the website.\n\n2. merge/link your Steam account to your VRChat account.\n\n3. delete your VRChat account. (I took a two-year break from VRChat)\n\n4. create a new VRChat account.\n\n5. try logging in with Steam to create a Steam-VRChat account for the linking process.\n\nMy request is that you please include a way to completely remove deleted account links / dead links from your database and give users the ability to relink their Steam account. If you are concerned that this will open the door to abuse, perhaps you can limit this to once a year. i would even be OK if we had to pay to have this resolved.",
